\begin{center}
{
\Large
Containers Quiz Practice Problems
}
\end{center}

\begin{note}
A \emph{container} is a class that holds other values.
The built-in containers you know are \lstinline{list}, \lstinline{dict}, \lstinline{set}, and \lstinline{tuple},
and they all implement the same small set of dunder methods---the \emph{container protocol}---so that the same syntax works on all of them.
In this notes packet we implement the container protocol on types we define ourselves:
a \lstinline{Range}, a linked list, and a binary search tree.
\end{note}

\begin{note}
Each problem produces exactly two lines of output and is worth two points,
one point per line.
Within each subsection the first problem is a correct reference
implementation. The remaining problems contain subtle bugs or variations,
so do not assume the code behaves like the corresponding built-in type---%
trace the code that is actually written.
\end{note}
